<title>RUSSIA: Russian oil firm SIDANKO 1996 net profit slumps.</title>
<headline>Russian oil firm SIDANKO 1996 net profit slumps.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31</p>
<p> (trln rbls)			   1996		     1995</p>
<p>Net sales</p>
<p>  (including joint ventures)     26.57		    19.03</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit</p>
<p>  (including joint ventures)	1.95			n/a</p>
<p>Net profit</p>
<p>  (including joint ventures)	0.68		     1.47</p>
<p>Oil production (million tonnes)</p>
<p>  (including joint ventures)     25.20		    26.90</p>
<p>Oil refining (million tonnes)</p>
<p>  (including joint ventures)     17.50		    20.00</p>
<p>Oil exports (million tonnes)</p>
<p>  (excluding joint ventures)	5.60		     6.50</p>
<p>Oil product exports (million tonnes)</p>
<p>  (excluding joint ventures)	4.90		     4.20</p>
<p>NOTES -- Full company name is OAO Sibirsko-Dalnevostochnaya Neftyanaya Kompaniya (SIDANKO). Figures prepared to Russian accounting standards on an accruals basis.</p>
<p>SIDANKO, a vertically integrated oil company whose production units include Kondpetroleum , Varyoganneftegaz  VJGZ.RTS and Chernogorneft, is Russia's fifth or sixth largest oil firm by output.</p>
<p>SIDANKO's main shareholder is the influential Uneximbank (Oneksimbank in Russian), with 34 percent of shares. Uneximbank said at the end of May it was considering selling the stake to attract investment in the company.</p>
<p>--Aleksandras Budrys, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
